{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Base Class.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Base Class.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"base class base class","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Base Class.md","fileName":"Base Class.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Base Class","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-06 20:37\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[Front-End Service Design]] [[C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["Front-End Service Design","C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc.pdf","aspnetcore3andangular9_3ed.pdf","c80andnetcore30moderncross-platformdevelopment.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Base Class.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Base Class.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"base class base class","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Base Class.md","fileName":"Base Class.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Base Class","heading":"Base Class","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A base class defines behavior or state intended to be inherited by more specialized classes. Shared form or service logic can be implemented once in the base and reused by multiple derived classes.\n\nThe base should contain only behavior common to its descendants. In the Angular examples, base form and data-service classes reduce duplicated validation and HTTP operations while subclasses retain entity-specific behavior.\n\nIn an inheritance hierarchy, the base class defines the state and behavior intended to be shared by more specific types. A sound is-a relationship requires a derived instance to remain usable wherever the base contract is expected.","tags":["baby"],"links":["Front-End Service Design","C Sharp Interfaces Generics and Inheritance","hands-onobject-orientedprogrammingwithc